(gate creaks)

1589
02:07:48,936 --> 02:07:50,927
(tubelight flickers)

1590
02:08:01,620 --> 02:08:03,230
(emotional music)

1591
02:08:23,835 --> 02:08:25,507
(soft instrumental music)

1592
02:08:38,273 --> 02:08:45,271
<i>♪ You laughed about
Calling me a joker ♪</i>

1593
02:08:45,702 --> 02:08:52,661
<i>♪ Now watch me play
Game's not over ♪</i>

1594
02:08:53,041 --> 02:08:59,581
<i>♪ In this twisted world
I’m dancing with danger ♪</i>

1595
02:09:00,363 --> 02:09:07,332
<i>♪ Betrayed, my soul is weak
You called me a joker ♪</i>

1596
02:09:07,878 --> 02:09:13,014
<i>♪ Pain is a part of me, forever ♪</i>

1597
02:09:15,211 --> 02:09:21,705
<i>♪ Pain drives me forward
Through the night ♪</i>

1598
02:09:22,628 --> 02:09:27,862
<i>♪ Pain wakes the life that I desire ♪</i>

1599
02:09:29,986 --> 02:09:33,503
<i>♪ Pain walks with me
A friend ♪</i>

1600
02:09:33,544 --> 02:09:38,955
<i>♪ So I'll survive ♪</i>

1601
02:09:39,481 --> 02:09:41,190
(music continues)

1602
02:10:05,011 --> 02:10:07,230
(music fades)

1603
02:10:08,310 --> 02:10:10,260
(opening song plays)

1604
02:10:19,818 --> 02:10:25,218
LABEL
WALK THE STAGE GLORIOUSLY

1605
02:10:28,403 --> 02:10:29,875
Motherfucker, let me see.

1606
02:10:30,293 --> 02:10:31,733
(kid) Hey, bastard, can't you see
me using it?

1607
02:10:36,347 --> 02:10:37,597
(banging rhythmically)

1608
02:10:43,408 --> 02:10:45,504
-(Prabha) I will take the change later.
-(man) Okay, Prabha!

1609
02:10:47,213 --> 02:10:51,773
(man) Hey, clean the table.
Can't you see people waiting?

1610
02:11:02,471 --> 02:11:04,013
(kid 1) Hey, fucker.

1611
02:11:04,573 --> 02:11:05,541
Hey.

1612
02:11:05,620 --> 02:11:06,593
What are you doing?

1613
02:11:06,760 --> 02:11:07,740
It is parked on its side-stand.

1614
02:11:07,854 --> 02:11:08,880
Hey, get down!

1615
02:11:09,041 --> 02:11:10,703
Hey, what are you playing at?
Move it.

1616
02:11:10,952 --> 02:11:12,433
Get down from my bike.

1617
02:11:12,740 --> 02:11:13,880
Can't you hear me?
Get down.

1618
02:11:13,906 --> 02:11:15,550
-Hey.
-You motherfucker!

1619
02:11:18,288 --> 02:11:19,383
Hey, get lost!

1620
02:11:20,032 --> 02:11:20,952
Move it.

1621
02:11:21,029 --> 02:11:22,481
(kid 1) Hey, dude.

1622
02:11:22,636 --> 02:11:23,615
-<i>Anna</i>, I'll see you later!
-(man) Okay.

1623
02:11:23,724 --> 02:11:24,718
-(knife swishes)
-(man) Hey.

1624
02:11:25,123 --> 02:11:26,102
-(boy grunts)
-(knife swishes)

1625
02:11:26,582 --> 02:11:27,570
(knife swishes)

1626
02:11:27,748 --> 02:11:28,779
(boy grunts)

1627
02:11:28,895 --> 02:11:30,281
Hey, who are you guys?

1628
02:11:30,542 --> 02:11:31,508
(kid 2) Don't let him get away.

1629
02:11:31,953 --> 02:11:33,040
Let's kill him!

1630
02:11:33,980 --> 02:11:34,940
(kid 1) Come on!

1631
02:11:36,717 --> 02:11:37,967
-(metal clacking)
-(knife swishes)

1632
02:11:38,660 --> 02:11:39,650
(kid 2) Motherfucker, you!

1633
02:11:39,672 --> 02:11:40,773
(grunts)

1634
02:11:41,016 --> 02:11:42,226
(dramatic music plays)

1635
02:11:42,402 --> 02:11:43,682
-(kid 1) Don't leave him!
-(kid 2) Come on, you.

1636
02:11:43,808 --> 02:11:46,095
-(kid 3) Mahesh, surround him.
-Motherfucker.

1637
02:11:46,117 --> 02:11:47,716
Listen to me.
You better leave.

1638
02:11:47,742 --> 02:11:48,815
(kid 4) Hit him!

1639
02:11:48,924 --> 02:11:50,375
(Prabha) What do you guys want?

1640
02:11:50,990 --> 02:11:52,109
Get lost!

1641
02:11:53,067 --> 02:11:54,197
-(kid 1) Get him.
-(Prabha) Hey.

1642
02:11:54,365 --> 02:11:55,744
(grunts)

1643
02:11:57,781 --> 02:11:59,322
-(grunts)
-(metal swishes)

1644
02:12:00,272 --> 02:12:02,885
-(kid 1) Come on, stab him!
-(kid 2) Stab that motherfucker.

1645
02:12:03,372 --> 02:12:04,498
-(kid 3) Motherfucking bastard.
-(kids grunt)

1646
02:12:05,073 --> 02:12:06,095
(kid 3) Kill this bastard!

1647
02:12:06,145 --> 02:12:07,366
-(grunts)
-(kid 3) Kill this motherfucker.

1648
02:12:08,504 --> 02:12:10,123
(grunts)

1649
02:12:11,814 --> 02:12:13,995
-(kid grunts)
-(kid 2) Motherfucker.

1650
02:12:15,695 --> 02:12:17,125
(grunts)

1651
02:12:18,322 --> 02:12:19,674
Bastard.

1652
02:12:19,685 --> 02:12:20,815
(grunts)

1653
02:12:21,215 --> 02:12:23,114
(kid grunts)

1654
02:12:26,655 --> 02:12:27,676
(kid) Motherfucker!

1655
02:12:28,556 --> 02:12:29,883
Come on.

1656
02:12:30,052 --> 02:12:30,993
(kid grunts)

1657
02:12:32,076 --> 02:12:33,137
(knife swishes)

1658
02:12:33,897 --> 02:12:35,246
(swishes)

1659
02:12:36,244 --> 02:12:37,734
(grunts)

1660
02:12:39,440 --> 02:12:41,690
Hey, bastards.
Get lost.

1661
02:12:41,709 --> 02:12:43,594
(kids grunt)

1662
02:12:43,653 --> 02:12:45,093
<i>Anna</i>, let go of me, please.

1663
02:12:45,407 --> 02:12:47,207
It hurts, <i>anna</i>.

1664
02:12:47,747 --> 02:12:49,427
<i>Anna</i>, please let me go.

1665
02:12:50,047 --> 02:12:51,036
Get lost!

1666
02:12:54,178 --> 02:12:56,076
(suspenseful music)

1667
02:13:13,823 --> 02:13:15,167
(knife swishes)

1668
02:13:15,251 --> 02:13:16,286
(motorbike whirrs)

1669
02:13:19,455 --> 02:13:20,717
(phone ringing)

1670
02:13:34,986 --> 02:13:35,954
Hello.

1671
02:13:37,767 --> 02:13:38,800
What's up, Prabhakaran?

1672
02:13:39,567 --> 02:13:42,031
I heard you were fighting with kids.

1673
02:13:44,373 --> 02:13:45,880
<i>Hope you didn't get hurt.</i>

1674
02:13:47,940 --> 02:13:49,013
They will not leave you.

1675
02:13:49,673 --> 02:13:52,606
Until you are stranded all alone,
they will never leave you.

1676
02:13:53,247 --> 02:13:54,526
<i>You have to keep running</i>.

1677
02:13:55,500 --> 02:13:57,300
A problem that was
caused by a Label

1678
02:13:57,613 --> 02:13:59,633
can be solved only by
another Label.

1679
02:14:00,524 --> 02:14:01,455
Well, sir.

1680
02:14:01,913 --> 02:14:02,973
As if they're the only bad people.

1681
02:14:03,237 --> 02:14:05,290
You are speaking with the audacity
of an innocent person?

1682
02:14:06,610 --> 02:14:07,810
Let me ask you this seriously.

1683
02:14:08,797 --> 02:14:10,110
How are you different from them?

1684
02:14:11,337 --> 02:14:12,516
Sir.

1685
02:14:13,123 --> 02:14:14,730
My fight itself is against all this.

1686
02:14:15,523 --> 02:14:16,490
Just because I have a problem now,

1687
02:14:17,217 --> 02:14:18,881
do you think I will go against it
and embrace their ways?

1688
02:14:20,317 --> 02:14:23,910
Who is your witness that makes
you take a dig at me?

1689
02:14:25,150 --> 02:14:26,330
Please hang up, sir.

1690
02:14:27,790 --> 02:14:29,390
(dramatic music)

1691
02:14:33,321 --> 02:14:34,550
(motorbike revs up)

1692
02:14:45,043 --> 02:14:46,255
(sirens blaring at a distance)

1693
02:14:49,180 --> 02:14:50,631
(music intensifies)

1694
02:14:57,591 --> 02:14:58,893
-(knife slashes)
-(man grunts)

1695
02:15:00,261 --> 02:15:01,469
-(Kumar shouts)
-(knife slashes)

1696
02:15:05,005 --> 02:15:07,792
Do you think he will
also get killed?

1697
02:15:08,997 --> 02:15:10,913
(Prabha) That won't happen.

1698
02:15:12,618 --> 02:15:14,298
(cameras clicking)

1699
02:15:19,202 --> 02:15:20,162
-(knife swishes)
-(boy grunts)

1700
02:15:25,701 --> 02:15:29,269
(intense music fades)

1701
02:15:35,777 --> 02:15:37,257
(Murugesan hisses)

1702
02:15:38,246 --> 02:15:39,575
(whispers) Hey.

1703
02:15:39,605 --> 02:15:41,810
Hey! (hisses intensely)

1704
02:15:42,859 --> 02:15:44,178
(Murugesan) Hey, Prabha.

1705
02:15:47,658 --> 02:15:49,149
(continues hissing)

1706
02:15:49,987 --> 02:15:51,445
Hey.

1707
02:15:51,713 --> 02:15:53,244
Hey, come here.

1708
02:15:53,556 --> 02:15:54,836
Oh, dear.

1709
02:15:56,010 --> 02:15:57,810
-Will they kill him as well?
-(knife slashes)

1710
02:15:58,192 --> 02:15:59,151
(boy grunts)

1711
02:16:01,125 --> 02:16:02,175
(hisses loudly)

1712
02:16:02,610 --> 02:16:04,610
Surround him. Don't let him go.

1713
02:16:05,397 --> 02:16:06,970
-(hisses)
-<i>(knife slashes, grunts)</i>

1714
02:16:07,585 --> 02:16:08,561
What is your problem, <i>Appa</i>?

1715
02:16:09,996 --> 02:16:11,185
-(dog barks)
-(cricket chirps)

1716
02:16:12,923 --> 02:16:14,296
(Amudha) Why did you have to
shout at him?

1717
02:16:14,757 --> 02:16:18,556
(Prabha) <i>Amma</i>, he was calling me
constantly when I was studying.

1718
02:16:18,873 --> 02:16:20,380
I just raised my voice at him
a little bit.

1719
02:16:20,829 --> 02:16:22,313
I wonder what kind of a husband
you raised.

1720
02:16:22,393 --> 02:16:24,054
I just raised my voice slightly,
and he left the house.

1721
02:16:24,112 --> 02:16:25,311
Stop it!

1722
02:16:25,327 --> 02:16:26,880
Now where will I look for him?

1723
02:16:28,318 --> 02:16:30,368
(waves crashing slowly)

1724
02:16:31,179 --> 02:16:32,750
-Hey!
-Huh?

1725
02:16:34,060 --> 02:16:35,666
(Amudha) What are you doing here?

1726
02:16:35,780 --> 02:16:37,252
Um.

1727
02:16:38,633 --> 02:16:39,756
Sorry, <i>Appa</i>!

1728
02:16:39,783 --> 02:16:40,728
Get lost.

1729
02:16:40,802 --> 02:16:41,772
Wow.

1730
02:16:42,022 --> 02:16:43,168
You could've just shown it
to me, right?

1731
02:16:43,862 --> 02:16:45,088
Why did you hiss at me and
annoy me?

1732
02:16:45,860 --> 02:16:48,127
Fine, <i>Amma</i> didn't see it.
You were discreet.

1733
02:16:48,555 --> 02:16:49,607
She didn't, did she?

1734
02:16:49,927 --> 02:16:51,924
-I hid it back there anyway.
-No, no. She didn't see it.

1735
02:16:52,393 --> 02:16:53,306
She didn't see.

1736
02:16:54,894 --> 02:16:56,142
What, man?

1737
02:16:56,841 --> 02:16:59,649
(peppy music playing)

1738
02:17:26,015 --> 02:17:26,215
HAPPY BIRTHDAY TO YOU

1739
02:17:26,275 --> 02:17:27,863
<i>♪ Oh, dear parrot ♪</i>

1740
02:17:28,143 --> 02:17:29,623
<i>♪ Oh, dear parrot ♪</i>

1741
02:17:29,990 --> 02:17:32,796
<i>♪ Hear my wish out and go ♪</i>

1742
02:17:33,703 --> 02:17:35,130
<i>♪ Deep in my heart ♪</i>

1743
02:17:35,321 --> 02:17:37,030
<i>♪ Tear it out ♪</i>

1744
02:17:37,270 --> 02:17:39,816
<i>♪ Take away my sorrow ♪</i>

1745
02:17:41,085 --> 02:17:43,665
<i>♪ I feel as light as a feather ♪</i>

1746
02:17:44,312 --> 02:17:47,381
<i>♪ Forgetting my age
When I see you ♪</i>

1747
02:17:48,488 --> 02:17:51,348
<i>♪ Sweet sounding, your anklet ♪</i>

1748
02:17:51,722 --> 02:17:55,074
<i>♪ Wash me over
With your glance ♪</i>

1749
02:17:55,382 --> 02:17:57,041
<i>♪ You are a golden nectar ♪</i>

1750
02:17:57,302 --> 02:17:58,928
<i>♪ As white as snow ♪</i>

1751
02:17:59,072 --> 02:18:03,861
<i>♪ You are my angel
The world hasn't seen yet ♪</i>

1752
02:18:04,115 --> 02:18:05,904
(peppy music continues)

1753
02:18:18,018 --> 02:18:19,378
<i>♪ Oh, dear parrot ♪</i>

1754
02:18:19,832 --> 02:18:21,325
<i>♪ Oh, dear parrot ♪</i>

1755
02:18:21,728 --> 02:18:24,655
<i>♪ Hear my wish out and go! ♪</i>

1756
02:18:25,428 --> 02:18:26,768
<i>♪ Deep in my heart ♪</i>

1757
02:18:27,208 --> 02:18:28,621
<i>♪ Tear it out ♪</i>

1758
02:18:28,868 --> 02:18:32,588
<i>♪ Take my sorrow away
And go ♪</i>

1759
02:18:32,648 --> 02:18:35,099
(chorus plays)

1760
02:18:47,450 --> 02:18:49,291
(instrumental music continues)

1761
02:19:01,888 --> 02:19:03,911
<i>♪ Shall I hold you? ♪</i>

1762
02:19:04,276 --> 02:19:05,989
<i>♪ Shall I live within you? ♪</i>

1763
02:19:06,315 --> 02:19:09,453
<i>♪ I want to catch hold of ♪</i>

1764
02:19:09,615 --> 02:19:13,373
<i>♪ Your thoughts and fill them up ♪</i>

1765
02:19:13,613 --> 02:19:16,882
<i>♪ Living for you is enough ♪</i>

1766
02:19:17,180 --> 02:19:20,439
<i>♪ A beauty like no other ♪</i>

1767
02:19:20,706 --> 02:19:24,292
<i>♪ I want to confess my love forever ♪</i>

1768
02:19:24,478 --> 02:19:25,971
<i>♪ This whole world ♪</i>

1769
02:19:26,178 --> 02:19:27,898
<i>♪ Should be in awe ♪</i>

1770
02:19:28,160 --> 02:19:31,100
<i>♪ Of our never-ending life ♪</i>

1771
02:19:31,333 --> 02:19:33,000
<i>♪ You are my dear ♪</i>

1772
02:19:33,287 --> 02:19:34,840
<i>♪ You are my beauty ♪</i>

1773
02:19:35,087 --> 02:19:39,456
<i>♪ You are my angel
The world hasn't seen yet! ♪</i>

1774
02:19:39,480 --> 02:19:41,312
(chorus plays)

1775
02:19:52,244 --> 02:19:54,236
(instrumental music stops)

1776
02:19:59,640 --> 02:20:02,767
"Case number 19 from Saroja
and Sakthivel.

1777
02:20:03,170 --> 02:20:04,448
"Thiruvallur street."

1778
02:20:07,377 --> 02:20:08,368
Please sit there.

1779
02:20:09,114 --> 02:20:11,203
"Chennai - 600004."

1780
02:20:11,477 --> 02:20:12,909
-Tell them both their hearing times.
-Okay.

1781
02:20:12,951 --> 02:20:14,092
-Don't delay.
-Okay, sir.

1782
02:20:14,445 --> 02:20:16,755
(Sukumar) Hey, tell me
that pin code again.

1783
02:20:17,056 --> 02:20:18,057
(Akhila) Wait.

1784
02:20:18,144 --> 02:20:20,043
600004.

1785
02:20:22,657 --> 02:20:23,843
<i>Akka</i>, please.

1786
02:20:24,290 --> 02:20:26,010
Don't ask me to bail them out.

1787
02:20:26,938 --> 02:20:28,291
Don't bail them out, son.

1788
02:20:30,125 --> 02:20:31,691
Let them stay inside.

1789
02:20:32,585 --> 02:20:33,565
Once they are out,

1790
02:20:33,898 --> 02:20:35,145
they might get a daily wage job

1791
02:20:35,392 --> 02:20:37,478
or find a job
as per their education.

1792
02:20:37,832 --> 02:20:38,791
Let them do whatever.

1793
02:20:39,548 --> 02:20:41,988
But don't let them come out,
make them feel important,

1794
02:20:42,375 --> 02:20:43,855
get into the Label,

1795
02:20:44,342 --> 02:20:45,981
and get them killed, Prabha.

1796
02:20:48,349 --> 02:20:49,276
We met them in prison.

1797
02:20:50,490 --> 02:20:52,670
They don't even have
an ounce of guilt, sir.

1798
02:20:53,437 --> 02:20:56,505
They were arrogantly walking around
as if they've achieved something great.

1799
02:20:57,028 --> 02:20:58,928
Policemen were saluting them.

1800
02:21:01,155 --> 02:21:02,501
They were relishing it, sir.

1801
02:21:03,475 --> 02:21:05,475
That adulation has
gone to their heads.

1802
02:21:07,842 --> 02:21:11,175
They consoled us saying they
will be out soon and not to worry.

1803
02:21:12,348 --> 02:21:14,081
(scoffs) In the euphoria
of getting a Label,

1804
02:21:14,702 --> 02:21:15,702
finally,

1805
02:21:16,130 --> 02:21:18,848
they've earned us a label of

1806
02:21:18,889 --> 02:21:21,380
being a mother and a sister
of murderers.

1807
02:21:22,744 --> 02:21:24,180
<i>Akka</i>.

1808
02:21:25,474 --> 02:21:26,493
I'll take care of it.

1809
02:21:28,738 --> 02:21:29,925
You can leave now.

1810
02:21:31,707 --> 02:21:34,489
(melodramatic music)

1811
02:21:44,029 --> 02:21:45,439
(firecrackers bursting)

1812
02:21:56,588 --> 02:21:59,455
(phone rings)

1813
02:22:03,408 --> 02:22:06,064
-Yes, <i>Amma</i>.
-<i>Thambi</i>, where are you?

1814
02:22:06,222 --> 02:22:07,341
I'm in my office.

1815
02:22:07,702 --> 02:22:09,961
<i>Appa</i> and I have come for
the temple festival. Are you coming?

1816
02:22:10,968 --> 02:22:12,101
No, <i>Amma</i>, I have some work.

1817
02:22:12,440 --> 02:22:13,409
I'll come later.

1818
02:22:13,555 --> 02:22:14,608
Oh, is it?

1819
02:22:14,952 --> 02:22:17,245
Okay, have your dinner
before coming home.

1820
02:22:17,767 --> 02:22:21,010
-Okay, <i>Amma</i>.
-Okay, then. I'm hanging up.

1821
02:22:21,388 --> 02:22:22,433
Here.

1822
02:22:23,276 --> 02:22:24,951
(exhales deeply)

1823
02:22:25,373 --> 02:22:26,721
(cracks knuckles)

1824
02:22:27,072 --> 02:22:28,384
(notification beeps)

1825
02:22:50,544 --> 02:22:52,669
(thrilling music)

1826
02:23:03,198 --> 02:23:04,612
(music intensifies)

1827
02:23:07,155 --> 02:23:10,008
We should have brought Poorni too.
She would've come to the temple.

1828
02:23:10,184 --> 02:23:11,628
-What say?
-(phone ringing)

1829
02:23:11,954 --> 02:23:13,322
-Hello.
-<i>Appa.</i>

1830
02:23:13,402 --> 02:23:14,856
Don't go anywhere.
I'm coming over.

1831
02:23:14,990 --> 02:23:16,563
-<i>Okay, we'll be right here.</i>
-<i>Appa</i>, stay with the crowd.

1832
02:23:16,897 --> 02:23:17,843
Don't go anywhere alone!

1833
02:23:18,303 --> 02:23:19,250
Why? What happened?

1834
02:23:19,262 --> 02:23:20,388
Hello?

1835
02:23:22,896 --> 02:23:25,190
Hello?
Hello--

1836
02:23:25,583 --> 02:23:28,003
-What happened? Is he coming?
-Yes, he said he's coming.

1837
02:23:31,031 --> 02:23:32,439
(motorbike whirrs)

1838
02:23:33,973 --> 02:23:36,801
-Listen, wait here. I'll be back.
-Where are you going?

1839
02:23:37,997 --> 02:23:39,155
I'm going to the restroom.

1840
02:23:40,649 --> 02:23:41,604
All right, go.

1841
02:23:47,254 --> 02:23:49,819
(drums playing)

1842
02:23:52,974 --> 02:23:54,808
(vehicles honk)

1843
02:23:55,346 --> 02:23:56,956
(festive drums playing)

1844
02:24:03,207 --> 02:24:04,950
Hold this. I'll be back.

1845
02:24:11,195 --> 02:24:14,425
(firecrackers continue bursting)

1846
02:24:22,049 --> 02:24:23,755
(motorbike screeches)

1847
02:24:37,242 --> 02:24:40,967
(ominous music)

1848
02:24:50,450 --> 02:24:51,986
-(knife swishes)
-(man grunts)

1849
02:24:52,411 --> 02:24:54,791
(thumps, whimpers)

1850
02:24:55,603 --> 02:24:57,206
(knife swishes)

1851
02:24:58,034 --> 02:24:58,884
(men shout)

1852
02:24:59,717 --> 02:25:03,000
(man grunts, shouts)

1853
02:25:11,979 --> 02:25:13,373
Hey.

1854
02:25:13,765 --> 02:25:15,111
Call the one who has sent you.

1855
02:25:17,023 --> 02:25:17,996
Do it!

1856
02:25:24,572 --> 02:25:25,951
Tell him that the one you all
came to kill

1857
02:25:26,732 --> 02:25:28,718
says he is Peter Label's Murugesan.

1858
02:25:29,085 --> 02:25:30,218
Ask him what has to be done.

1859
02:25:30,722 --> 02:25:31,664
Ask him!

1860
02:25:34,607 --> 02:25:36,566
(man) <i>Hey, leave immediately!</i>

1861
02:25:40,012 --> 02:25:41,205
Run away.

1862
02:25:42,159 --> 02:25:44,230
(intimidating music)

1863
02:25:53,887 --> 02:25:55,154
-(music stops)
-(feet shuffling)

1864
02:25:57,493 --> 02:25:58,493
-Shall we go?
-Let's go.

1865
02:26:01,370 --> 02:26:03,183
-As if you'll starve.
-Yes.

1866
02:26:03,550 --> 02:26:05,633
-Make fish curry--
-<i>Appa, Amma</i>.

1867
02:26:05,989 --> 02:26:07,149
<i>Appa</i>.

1868
02:26:07,412 --> 02:26:08,570
Are you all right, <i>Appa</i>?

1869
02:26:08,732 --> 02:26:09,743
Yes.
Why? What's wrong?

1870
02:26:10,872 --> 02:26:11,931
No, it's nothing.

1871
02:26:13,109 --> 02:26:14,126
Let's go, <i>Appa</i>.

1872
02:26:14,132 --> 02:26:16,165
Do one thing, take your mother.
Be safe.

1873
02:26:16,500 --> 02:26:17,686
Give me your bike key.

1874
02:26:20,938 --> 02:26:23,205
-You guys go. I'll be right back.
-Okay, <i>Appa</i>.

1875
02:26:26,752 --> 02:26:29,051
-Why is he going alone?
-Nothing, <i>Amma</i>, he will come.

1876
02:26:29,411 --> 02:26:30,535
(train horn blows)

1877
02:26:36,258 --> 02:26:37,158
(Amudha) What happened?

1878
02:26:38,825 --> 02:26:39,904
(Prabha) Nothing, <i>Amma</i>.

1879
02:26:40,272 --> 02:26:42,338
I'm just thinking about a case.

1880
02:26:43,752 --> 02:26:46,098
Four men came at us
with knives at the festival.

1881
02:26:47,132 --> 02:26:49,105
When I came out of the restroom,

1882
02:26:49,653 --> 02:26:53,020
they were shoving their knives in
their pockets and running away.

1883
02:26:53,300 --> 02:26:55,206
My heart skipped a beat
when I saw it.

1884
02:26:56,287 --> 02:26:57,453
Thankfully, you showed up.

1885
02:26:58,113 --> 02:27:00,524
I don't know what happened
or what the problem was.

1886
02:27:02,635 --> 02:27:03,598
It is nothing!

1887
02:27:03,674 --> 02:27:05,491
<i>Appa</i> was standing
in the corner, right?

1888
02:27:06,185 --> 02:27:07,465
They may have come
to rob people.

1889
02:27:08,392 --> 02:27:09,392
And they ran away after
seeing <i>Appa</i>.

1890
02:27:09,905 --> 02:27:11,401
(Amudha) Could be so.

1891
02:27:12,955 --> 02:27:14,015
I was terribly scared.

1892
02:27:16,515 --> 02:27:19,433
(music turns upbeat)

1893
02:27:36,222 --> 02:27:37,515
(Paramasivan) <i>They will not
leave you.</i>

1894
02:27:37,982 --> 02:27:40,855
<i>Until you are stranded all alone,
they will never leave you.</i>

1895
02:27:41,542 --> 02:27:43,035
<i>You'll have to keep running.</i>

1896
02:27:44,695 --> 02:27:47,066
(music intensifies)

1897
02:28:01,305 --> 02:28:03,174
(phone ringing)

1898
02:28:11,561 --> 02:28:13,625
Welcome, Prabhakaran.

1899
02:28:13,748 --> 02:28:15,074
Welcome.

1900
02:28:16,242 --> 02:28:17,168
What is the case, sir?

1901
02:28:18,675 --> 02:28:20,481
It is your boys' case, of course.

1902
02:28:21,075 --> 02:28:22,457
Veera and Kumar.

1903
02:28:25,667 --> 02:28:28,601
(emotional music)

1904
02:28:33,928 --> 02:28:35,032
One tea.

1905
02:28:43,935 --> 02:28:45,991
-Sorry, sir.
-It's okay.

1906
02:28:56,432 --> 02:28:57,572
Miss.

1907
02:28:57,583 --> 02:28:59,519
Prabha--
Prabhakaran, miss.

1908
02:29:00,150 --> 02:29:01,172
I was your student.

1909
02:29:03,937 --> 02:29:05,536
I used to come from Vaali Nagar.

1910
02:29:08,323 --> 02:29:11,796
You asked me what I wanted to become,
and I asked you to help me know.

1911
02:29:13,089 --> 02:29:14,646
Hey!

1912
02:29:15,023 --> 02:29:16,530
Are you that Prabha?

1913
02:29:17,230 --> 02:29:18,156
What are you doing now?

1914
02:29:18,850 --> 02:29:20,650
-Are you a lawyer now?
-Yes, miss.

1915
02:29:20,680 --> 02:29:21,612
Very good, son!

1916
02:29:21,690 --> 02:29:22,630
What are you doing here, miss?

1917
02:29:22,717 --> 02:29:23,648
Well...

1918
02:29:23,743 --> 02:29:27,285
A counsellor is using our school
ground as a cycle stand...

1919
02:29:27,538 --> 02:29:28,763
Forget it.
Have a seat.

1920
02:29:31,670 --> 02:29:32,602
So?

1921
02:29:33,615 --> 02:29:35,475
Are you really going
to become the judge?

1922
02:29:36,127 --> 02:29:38,711
In another six to seven months,
I will be, miss.

1923
02:29:39,575 --> 02:29:40,631
Oh, my!

1924
02:29:41,245 --> 02:29:42,711
-Fantastic, boy!
-(chuckles)

1925
02:29:42,922 --> 02:29:47,688
I thought you were just excited and
might take up a normal job.

1926
02:29:49,067 --> 02:29:50,933
You are going on the right track.

1927
02:29:51,887 --> 02:29:52,986
You have made me proud.

1928
02:29:53,101 --> 02:29:54,147
Thank you, miss.

1929
02:29:55,060 --> 02:29:56,060
This is your Label.

1930
02:29:57,087 --> 02:29:59,381
You will definitely change
the identity of your area.

1931
02:30:01,738 --> 02:30:03,360
I should see you as a judge
very soon.

1932
02:30:03,813 --> 02:30:04,889
I want to feel prouder.

1933
02:30:06,007 --> 02:30:09,246
On our school's annual day next year,
you will be the chief guest.

1934
02:30:09,761 --> 02:30:12,139
I will introduce you as the
"Honourable Judge Prabhakaran"

1935
02:30:12,557 --> 02:30:15,167
to everyone in school.

1936
02:30:15,760 --> 02:30:17,227
It has a nice ring to it,
doesn't it?

1937
02:30:24,342 --> 02:30:26,064
(solemn music)

1938
02:30:26,680 --> 02:30:30,673
(teacher) <i>On stage, I will proudly
tell the whole school about you.</i>

1939
02:30:31,113 --> 02:30:33,740
<i>What happened to you,
how it changed you,</i>

1940
02:30:34,053 --> 02:30:35,987
<i>what you asked me in class,</i>

1941
02:30:36,352 --> 02:30:38,065
<i>what you have become today,</i>

1942
02:30:38,452 --> 02:30:39,351
<i>I should tell them everything.</i>

1943
02:30:39,755 --> 02:30:41,681
<i>You will be an inspiration
to all the students.</i>

1944
02:30:42,208 --> 02:30:43,501
<i>There will be many more
like you.</i>

1945
02:30:44,275 --> 02:30:45,935
<i>I'm immensely proud of you.</i>

1946
02:30:46,655 --> 02:30:48,721
<i>As "the Honourable
Judge Prabhakaran,"</i>

1947
02:30:49,115 --> 02:30:51,601
I should present you on the stage.

1948
02:30:52,322 --> 02:30:53,808
It has a nice ring to it,
doesn't it?

1949
02:30:56,051 --> 02:30:58,187
(teacher) <i>You made my day.</i>

1950
02:30:58,468 --> 02:30:59,628
<i>What more do I need</i>?

1951
02:30:59,844 --> 02:31:01,534
<i>I'll see you, boy.</i>

1952
02:31:01,576 --> 02:31:02,679
<i>Sorry.</i>

1953
02:31:02,767 --> 02:31:03,733
<i>See you later, Your Honour!</i>

1954
02:31:04,320 --> 02:31:06,420
(man) Veerasekhar and Kumaraguru
versus Arul Kumaran.

1955
02:31:06,824 --> 02:31:09,355
Veerasekhar and Kumaraguru
versus Arul Kumaran.

1956
02:31:09,495 --> 02:31:11,957
Veerasekhar and Kumaraguru
versus Arul Kumaran.

1957
02:31:14,448 --> 02:31:16,528
(music intensifies)

1958
02:31:22,662 --> 02:31:23,741
You are making a mistake, <i>thambi</i>.

1959
02:31:24,042 --> 02:31:25,161
Aren't you a lawyer?

1960
02:31:25,500 --> 02:31:27,980
I'm asking you to do your job.
What is the problem now?

1961
02:31:28,707 --> 02:31:30,373
<i>You can take up Ayya's cases,</i>

1962
02:31:30,863 --> 02:31:32,310
earn good money,

1963
02:31:32,607 --> 02:31:34,483
and be happy in life.

1964
02:31:35,490 --> 02:31:36,523
That guy is also a lawyer, right?

1965
02:31:37,058 --> 02:31:37,995
<i>Who?</i>

1966
02:31:38,658 --> 02:31:39,938
Him, your Ayya.

1967
02:31:43,578 --> 02:31:45,151
Ask him to work for me.

1968
02:31:45,905 --> 02:31:48,398
Let him take up some good cases
before his time comes.

1969
02:31:49,965 --> 02:31:52,151
His reaction will be
totally adverse.

1970
02:31:52,798 --> 02:31:53,798
Adverse?

1971
02:31:55,818 --> 02:31:57,088
That man is a criminal.

1972
02:31:57,778 --> 02:31:59,458
If his reaction is going
to be adverse,

1973
02:32:00,871 --> 02:32:02,017
I'm a criminal lawyer.

1974
02:32:02,458 --> 02:32:05,213
(music rises)

1975
