-Sir...
-(policeman) Move aside.

2097
02:41:14,811 --> 02:41:17,519
-Hey, move aside. Leave.
-(Veera) Hold on, man.

2098
02:41:18,261 --> 02:41:19,641
(crowd cheering)

2099
02:41:20,155 --> 02:41:22,188
-(policeman) Move aside!
-(Veera) Sir!

2100
02:41:22,451 --> 02:41:23,753
-(men whistling)
-(clapping)

2101
02:41:25,542 --> 02:41:26,609
-(crowd roars with joy)
-(Veera) Thanks, sir.

2102
02:41:27,596 --> 02:41:29,526
(Kumar) Awesome, sir.
Thank you so much.

2103
02:41:30,305 --> 02:41:31,583
(loud cheering, clapping)

2104
02:41:31,924 --> 02:41:33,364
Hey, <i>anna</i>.
Come on.

2105
02:41:33,444 --> 02:41:34,894
Have a look at
our <i>anna's</i> gift for you.

2106
02:41:36,223 --> 02:41:38,437
-Sir, give us a moment.
-Excuse us, sir.

2107
02:41:42,302 --> 02:41:43,481
(Veera) Hey, what's this, man?

2108
02:41:44,411 --> 02:41:46,093
-(Kumar) Awesome, isn't it?
-(Veera) Look at this.

2109
02:41:48,269 --> 02:41:50,418
-(music dies down)
-(indistinct chatter)

2110
02:41:53,448 --> 02:41:56,191
(crowd cheering, whistling)

2111
02:41:59,450 --> 02:42:01,069
(opening music)

2112
02:42:11,196 --> 02:42:16,145
LABEL
WALK THE STAGE GLORIOUSLY

2113
02:42:18,302 --> 02:42:20,302
(rousing music)

2114
02:42:33,700 --> 02:42:34,706
(whistle blows)

2115
02:42:35,224 --> 02:42:36,614
(cheering, clapping)

2116
02:42:53,750 --> 02:42:55,663
(music turns sombre)

2117
02:42:58,750 --> 02:43:00,588
He flies like a string-less kite.

2118
02:43:00,681 --> 02:43:04,590
If he continues to train, he will make
it to the Commonwealth this year.

2119
02:43:05,707 --> 02:43:08,967
He is on fire as if to finish
something or get somewhere.

2120
02:43:09,334 --> 02:43:10,952
Be happy.

2121
02:43:11,554 --> 02:43:14,264
He is running at full speed
on the right track. (chuckles)

2122
02:43:19,056 --> 02:43:20,763
(bike whirring)

2123
02:43:26,580 --> 02:43:28,891
(menacing music)

2124
02:43:32,213 --> 02:43:33,863
(motorbike revving)

2125
02:43:40,159 --> 02:43:41,195
Here, take it.

2126
02:43:57,508 --> 02:43:58,714
<i>Amma.</i>

2127
02:44:00,626 --> 02:44:02,157
-Give it.
-(woman) There's curry inside.

2128
02:44:04,639 --> 02:44:06,119
Hey, what do you want?

2129
02:44:06,159 --> 02:44:08,020
<i>Akka</i>, give me two <i>vadas</i>
and <i>bajji</i>.

2130
02:44:10,176 --> 02:44:11,312
<i>Amma.</i>

2131
02:44:12,936 --> 02:44:14,365
(music turns tense)

2132
02:44:16,883 --> 02:44:18,515
(phone ringing)

2133
02:44:24,494 --> 02:44:25,498
Take it.

2134
02:44:31,084 --> 02:44:33,291
(music intensifies)

2135
02:44:38,228 --> 02:44:39,260
<i>Akka.</i>

2136
02:44:39,927 --> 02:44:41,151
Did she give you a key?

2137
02:44:42,016 --> 02:44:46,103
She packed all her things and
vacated the house long ago.

2138
02:44:47,948 --> 02:44:49,329
Didn't she tell you?

2139
02:44:55,036 --> 02:44:56,290
<i>Amma.</i>

2140
02:44:57,707 --> 02:44:59,385
(suspenseful music)

2141
02:45:03,565 --> 02:45:05,463
(music rises)

2142
02:45:16,025 --> 02:45:16,977
(music dies down)

2143
02:45:22,600 --> 02:45:24,180
(bike revs up)

2144
02:45:37,219 --> 02:45:39,587
(music turns sinister)

2145
02:45:59,346 --> 02:46:01,376
(rousing music)

2146
02:46:05,884 --> 02:46:07,302
(water splashes)

2147
02:46:18,164 --> 02:46:19,622
(music dips)

2148
02:46:25,748 --> 02:46:28,478
(music rising)

2149
02:46:42,386 --> 02:46:43,575
(eerie music)

2150
02:46:45,803 --> 02:46:47,863
(man) Remain silent
until the discussion is over.

2151
02:46:48,003 --> 02:46:49,771
(indistinct chatter)

2152
02:46:50,736 --> 02:46:52,859
(man) Hey, listen to me.

2153
02:46:53,544 --> 02:46:54,544
-Let me talk.
-(sniffs)

2154
02:46:56,460 --> 02:46:57,871
(suspenseful music)

2155
02:47:12,102 --> 02:47:15,070
(riveting music)

2156
02:47:24,497 --> 02:47:25,520
What's up, Arul?

2157
02:47:25,566 --> 02:47:26,724
What brings you here?

2158
02:47:27,514 --> 02:47:29,936
Well, <i>Anna</i>...
My brother is no more.

2159
02:47:30,649 --> 02:47:34,027
Whom should we talk to now?
Who's next in power?

2160
02:47:36,433 --> 02:47:39,963
As long as Paathaalam was there,
no man in his area dared to act up.

2161
02:47:44,690 --> 02:47:46,052
(exhales)

2162
02:47:47,195 --> 02:47:49,095
Paathaalam didn't let that happen.

2163
02:47:51,365 --> 02:47:53,346
Bloody hell! He was stabbed
in the middle of the road!

2164
02:47:53,621 --> 02:47:54,760
Instead of killing those bastards,

2165
02:47:55,356 --> 02:47:56,962
you're here to compete for
Paathalam's spot?

2166
02:47:57,352 --> 02:47:58,954
Don't you feel ashamed?
(spits)

2167
02:47:59,860 --> 02:48:01,481
We are looking for those boys.

2168
02:48:01,665 --> 02:48:02,982
Had that lawyer Prabhakaran
not come in our way--

2169
02:48:03,016 --> 02:48:03,444
Hey!

2170
02:48:03,640 --> 02:48:05,111
What are you talking about, Arul?

2171
02:48:05,169 --> 02:48:06,399
What nonsense!

2172
02:48:06,674 --> 02:48:09,801
You think you can justify Paathaalam's
death by killing those bastards?

2173
02:48:11,190 --> 02:48:12,700
Was that all Paathaalam meant
to us?

2174
02:48:15,398 --> 02:48:16,691
It's wrong, Arul.

2175
02:48:17,478 --> 02:48:18,683
This is bad.

2176
02:48:21,077 --> 02:48:24,939
We shouldn't cut the tail,
but the dick.

2177
02:48:26,088 --> 02:48:27,547
Bunk Suresh.

2178
02:48:28,231 --> 02:48:29,526
Bitch! We have to finish him off!

2179
02:48:30,975 --> 02:48:32,297
Aadhi.

2180
02:48:34,923 --> 02:48:40,006
For what happened, we must make
that Ayya bastard pee his pants!

2181
02:48:40,378 --> 02:48:43,672
Before his pants dry, we cut off
his dick and leave him in agony!

2182
02:48:43,981 --> 02:48:45,162
Yes, <i>anna</i>.

2183
02:48:45,754 --> 02:48:46,743
(sinister music)

2184
02:48:48,165 --> 02:48:51,885
Paathaalam didn't leave a hole
that any damn guy can fill.

2185
02:48:53,741 --> 02:48:55,173
He has left a valley behind.

2186
02:48:59,057 --> 02:49:01,206
Hey! (snapping fingers)
Listen up!

2187
02:49:02,093 --> 02:49:05,424
The one that slaughters Bunk Suresh
will be the next in power!

2188
02:49:06,427 --> 02:49:07,921
Fuckers.

2189
02:49:07,978 --> 02:49:10,261
Look at these motherfuckers.

2190
02:49:10,588 --> 02:49:11,948
Assholes.

2191
02:49:12,185 --> 02:49:15,731
(music rises)

2192
02:49:16,585 --> 02:49:17,665
-(music stops)
-(Prabha) Enough, <i>Amma</i>.

2193
02:49:18,940 --> 02:49:20,119
(Amudha) Have some sambhar.

2194
02:49:21,433 --> 02:49:23,259
<i>Akka</i>, hold on.
Hold on.

2195
02:49:23,300 --> 02:49:24,242
-(Amudha) What is it?
-Come on.

2196
02:49:24,322 --> 02:49:26,042
Are you trying to soften him up
by serving him sambhar?

2197
02:49:26,366 --> 02:49:27,918
-Have this.
-What's this, <i>akka</i>?

2198
02:49:28,323 --> 02:49:30,270
-Chicken curry.
-Oh!

2199
02:49:30,422 --> 02:49:31,684
Pass me the ladle, <i>akka</i>.

2200
02:49:33,153 --> 02:49:35,766
Thank God, I came at the right time.

2201
02:49:35,872 --> 02:49:37,504
-Here, have some.
-Enough, <i>akka</i>.

2202
02:49:38,043 --> 02:49:39,585
(vessel clatters)

2203
02:49:40,677 --> 02:49:41,943
-Will you join them too?
-No, <i>akka</i>.

2204
02:49:41,985 --> 02:49:43,696
-Let the boy eat.
-Serve some for <i>Appa</i>.

2205
02:49:44,591 --> 02:49:45,651
Dear.

2206
02:49:46,933 --> 02:49:47,973
Just a little.

2207
02:49:51,537 --> 02:49:52,628
-How is it?
-Mmm!

2208
02:49:52,790 --> 02:49:53,838
Yummy!

2209
02:49:53,855 --> 02:49:55,103
It's good, right?

2210
02:49:55,362 --> 02:49:56,852
It came out well today, <i>akka</i>.

2211
02:49:59,280 --> 02:50:00,350
(sentimental music)

2212
02:50:02,569 --> 02:50:04,315
What is it, <i>akka?</i>
Do you have anything to tell me?

2213
02:50:04,843 --> 02:50:06,304
It's nothing. Just eat.

2214
02:50:10,004 --> 02:50:13,164
(referee) <i>He's on fire, as if to
finish something or get somewhere.</i>

2215
02:50:13,640 --> 02:50:15,142
<i>Be happy.</i>

2216
02:50:15,662 --> 02:50:18,312
<i>He is running at full speed
on the right track.</i>

2217
02:50:25,237 --> 02:50:27,019
(Aadhi exhales with difficulty)

2218
02:50:29,181 --> 02:50:30,196
(trainer) Come on.

2219
02:50:30,345 --> 02:50:31,956
Last four.

2220
02:50:32,124 --> 02:50:33,255
Come on. Come on.

2221
02:50:33,998 --> 02:50:35,038
Come on.

2222
02:50:35,608 --> 02:50:37,078
Last three. Easy.

2223
02:50:38,263 --> 02:50:39,695
-(woman) Morning, sir.
-(phone ringing)

2224
02:50:42,575 --> 02:50:44,306
(sinister music)

2225
02:50:45,555 --> 02:50:47,215
-(trainer) Last two.
-(man) <i>Anna</i>.

2226
02:50:47,226 --> 02:50:48,725
Bunk Suresh got released.

2227
02:50:51,789 --> 02:50:52,790
(gate creaking)

2228
02:51:00,369 --> 02:51:02,030
(breathes shakily)

2229
02:51:13,106 --> 02:51:15,155
(rousing music)

2230
02:51:40,209 --> 02:51:41,759
(car engine starts)

2231
02:52:01,693 --> 02:52:03,023
(tyres screech)

2232
02:52:05,018 --> 02:52:07,933
-(music rises)

2233
02:52:09,967 --> 02:52:10,982
-(music stops)

2234
02:52:15,848 --> 02:52:17,182
-(Prabha) Hi.
-Hi.

2235
02:52:17,421 --> 02:52:19,723
What's with this sudden treat?

2236
02:52:20,066 --> 02:52:21,411
I resigned from my job.

2237
02:52:21,419 --> 02:52:23,539
So, I called to give you a treat.

2238
02:52:24,266 --> 02:52:25,358
Oh.

2239
02:52:25,477 --> 02:52:26,884
Why?

2240
02:52:27,262 --> 02:52:29,371
I've been thinking about this
for a while now.

2241
02:52:29,614 --> 02:52:31,276
The pressure at the office
is unbearable.

2242
02:52:31,393 --> 02:52:35,013
They don't want us to cover the mistakes
of the people they need.

2243
02:52:35,077 --> 02:52:37,573
But if their opponents
make a small mistake,

2244
02:52:37,668 --> 02:52:39,501
they don't mind starting
even a debate show about it.

2245
02:52:39,593 --> 02:52:41,309
God! I just couldn't take it!

2246
02:52:42,284 --> 02:52:43,282
(sighs)

2247
02:52:43,502 --> 02:52:45,499
So, I'm planning to start
a digital channel

2248
02:52:45,756 --> 02:52:48,318
and practise
the kind of journalism I wish.

2249
02:52:49,922 --> 02:52:51,104
Super, Mahi.

2250
02:52:51,757 --> 02:52:52,917
Can I say something?

2251
02:52:53,252 --> 02:52:56,651
The moment you start talking
about what's important,

2252
02:52:56,971 --> 02:52:59,379
you won't find even a single
person to listen to it at first.

2253
02:52:59,907 --> 02:53:01,659
But that doesn't mean
you shouldn't talk about it.

2254
02:53:02,091 --> 02:53:04,460
Only then will someone give us
an ear someday.

2255
02:53:06,898 --> 02:53:08,477
I know it's going to be hard.

2256
02:53:08,789 --> 02:53:10,126
But there's no other way.

2257
02:53:10,909 --> 02:53:11,936
All the best!

2258
02:53:16,138 --> 02:53:19,073
Prabha, how are you going
to solve the case?

2259
02:53:21,466 --> 02:53:22,506
Why?

2260
02:53:22,535 --> 02:53:24,175
Is this your first content?

2261
02:53:24,765 --> 02:53:25,907
(laughs)

2262
02:53:30,357 --> 02:53:31,667
(liquid pouring)

2263
02:53:32,327 --> 02:53:34,115
(people chattering)

2264
02:53:37,666 --> 02:53:38,881
Okay.
Okay, sir.

2265
02:53:39,501 --> 02:53:40,642
No issues.
We'll take care of it.

2266
02:53:41,005 --> 02:53:42,166
Okay, sir.

2267
02:53:43,124 --> 02:53:45,185
What was the name?
Ista...?

2268
02:53:45,205 --> 02:53:46,573
Istagasa.

2269
02:53:46,859 --> 02:53:48,339
Istagasa. What does it mean?

2270
02:53:48,916 --> 02:53:52,716
See, there are only two ways to
register a criminal case in India.

2271
02:53:53,135 --> 02:53:55,311
One way is to go to the station

2272
02:53:55,600 --> 02:53:57,240
and file a complaint
under CrPC Section 154.

2273
02:53:57,329 --> 02:54:02,382
Or as per CrPC Section 156
Subclass-3 under Section 200,

2274
02:54:02,518 --> 02:54:05,298
we can go directly to the Judicial
Magistrate and file a complaint.

2275
02:54:05,339 --> 02:54:07,473
-Okay.
-That's called Istagasa.

2276
02:54:08,026 --> 02:54:09,207
Oh.

2277
02:54:10,799 --> 02:54:15,536
Also, there's no use complaining
about a policeman at the station.

2278
02:54:15,702 --> 02:54:16,647
(both laugh)

2279
02:54:16,765 --> 02:54:17,772
It's all a game.

2280
02:54:17,855 --> 02:54:19,364
It will go in vain.

2281
02:54:19,376 --> 02:54:22,527
But a complaint to the Magistrate
will not be in vain.

2282
02:54:22,637 --> 02:54:26,705
This is one reason
why the Police fear and resent us.

2283
02:54:26,865 --> 02:54:30,762
And, for us, this is going to be
one tough Istagasa.

2284
02:54:30,911 --> 02:54:31,970
(laughs)

2285
02:54:32,944 --> 02:54:35,949
They've filed a false case
against a lawyer.

2286
02:54:36,220 --> 02:54:38,210
Do you think the other cases
might not have been false?

2287
02:54:38,229 --> 02:54:41,928
Our sir has dug out
all such false cases.

2288
02:54:46,387 --> 02:54:48,901
<i>All those cases are going to
the judge's table.</i>

2289
02:54:48,928 --> 02:54:51,808
(distorted male voice) Order.
Order. Order.

2290
02:54:56,231 --> 02:54:58,402
(inspiring song)

2291
02:55:07,891 --> 02:55:12,755
WHAT DOES A MAN FROM WISDOM GAIN,
IF HE PINES NOT AT OTHERS' PAIN?

2292
02:55:22,955 --> 02:55:25,176
(man) <i> Case number 24/206.</i>

2293
02:55:25,522 --> 02:55:27,685
Elangovan, State of Tamil Nadu.

2294
02:55:27,769 --> 02:55:28,988
Go.

2295
02:55:29,608 --> 02:55:30,739
(music fades out)

2296
02:55:34,787 --> 02:55:36,808
(introspective music)

2297
02:55:37,635 --> 02:55:39,345
The accused is present, Your Honour.

2298
02:55:39,366 --> 02:55:40,555
And the defence?

2299
02:55:40,585 --> 02:55:42,475
Guilty, Your Honour.
He has surrendered.

2300
02:55:43,006 --> 02:55:44,584
(judge) Well?
Do you accept?

2301
02:55:44,928 --> 02:55:46,000
Yes, sir.

2302
02:55:46,104 --> 02:55:48,632
Six months in jail.
Rs. 50,000 to be paid as fine.

2303
02:55:48,880 --> 02:55:51,520
If you fail to pay, you'll have to
stay in jail for three more months.

2304
02:55:52,025 --> 02:55:53,305
I'll remain in jail, sir.

2305
02:55:55,087 --> 02:55:56,257
Next.

2306
02:55:56,648 --> 02:55:58,882
Case number 26/207.

2307
02:55:59,038 --> 02:56:00,885
Arul Kumaran vs Prabhakaran.

2308
02:56:02,438 --> 02:56:04,209
(music turns tense)

2309
02:56:09,899 --> 02:56:11,459
Accused present, Your Honour.

2310
02:56:16,451 --> 02:56:18,243
The petitioner
couldn't make it today.

2311
02:56:18,265 --> 02:56:20,643
He's not well. He has been admitted
to the hospital.

2312
02:56:20,727 --> 02:56:22,086
(glasses clink)

2313
02:56:23,689 --> 02:56:25,529
We've produced the AR copy for that.

2314
02:56:26,639 --> 02:56:28,350
Requesting another date,
Your Honour.

2315
02:56:29,548 --> 02:56:30,897
The 15th of next month.

2316
02:56:31,128 --> 02:56:32,689
Thank you, My Lord.

2317
02:56:35,882 --> 02:56:37,309
-(music rises)

2318
02:56:57,443 --> 02:56:58,470
-(music stops)

2319
02:56:58,765 --> 02:57:00,509
-Akhila, how will you go? By bike?
-Yes, by bike.

2320
02:57:00,733 --> 02:57:01,773
-Okay.
-(Akhila) Sir.

2321
02:57:01,784 --> 02:57:02,825
We'll leave now. Bye.

2322
02:57:02,962 --> 02:57:05,252
-What about you, sir?
-It will take some time. You may leave.

2323
02:57:05,273 --> 02:57:06,393
-Okay, sir.
-Bye, sir.

2324
02:57:09,973 --> 02:57:11,482
(sinister music)

2325
02:57:17,934 --> 02:57:19,025
(Arul) Sir.

2326
02:57:24,064 --> 02:57:25,099
Move, please.

2327
02:57:30,993 --> 02:57:32,052
Take a seat, sir.

2328
02:57:32,314 --> 02:57:33,645
I want to talk to you, sir.

2329
02:57:34,686 --> 02:57:36,565
This might sound a bit old-school.

2330
02:57:37,486 --> 02:57:39,514
But it feels right to say it now.

2331
02:57:40,932 --> 02:57:43,025
Let's talk only during
court proceedings.

2332
02:57:44,520 --> 02:57:45,448
(tuts)

2333
02:57:45,932 --> 02:57:47,534
Please do something, sir.

2334
02:57:48,256 --> 02:57:50,376
Well, you already seem on edge.

2335
02:57:52,652 --> 02:57:55,522
The Magistrate will retire
in four months.

2336
02:57:56,152 --> 02:57:59,026
Until then, I will drag the case
out with some silly excuses like

2337
02:57:59,060 --> 02:58:01,889
I am unwell, I'm out of town or
my grandpa kicked the bucket.

2338
02:58:02,825 --> 02:58:04,283
Then, a new judge will come.

2339
02:58:04,594 --> 02:58:07,476
The investigation will restart.

2340
02:58:07,583 --> 02:58:10,156
So, this might take at least
two or three years, sir.

2341
02:58:14,337 --> 02:58:17,942
It isn't to show you the consequences
of messing with a lawyer.

2342
02:58:18,933 --> 02:58:21,604
If you think it is easy to ruin
a person's life by filing a false case,

2343
02:58:22,564 --> 02:58:24,782
you can also ruin the complainant
using the same case.

2344
02:58:25,393 --> 02:58:26,583
Wow!

2345
02:58:26,868 --> 02:58:28,499
This is a bit new to you, right?

2346
02:58:29,063 --> 02:58:30,604
I didn't file the case, sir.

2347
02:58:34,045 --> 02:58:36,655
I was given
your juvenile case details.

2348
02:58:36,847 --> 02:58:39,055
They said we could use the details
to file such a case.

2349
02:58:41,824 --> 02:58:43,420
They wanted me to file the case.

2350
02:58:44,279 --> 02:58:46,180
Who?
Senguttuvan?

2351
02:58:52,653 --> 02:58:54,012
Ayya...

2352
02:58:57,690 --> 02:59:01,469
(music intensifies)

2353
02:59:21,930 --> 02:59:23,583
I told you.

2354
02:59:23,844 --> 02:59:25,545
There will be consequences.

2355
02:59:26,934 --> 02:59:29,105
The guy who filed a case
in the bar council, right?

2356
02:59:31,406 --> 02:59:32,831
Join the Label.

2357
02:59:33,324 --> 02:59:36,785
You can sponsor
and run your own tournament.

2358
02:59:38,093 --> 02:59:40,143
(inhales sharply, sighs)

2359
02:59:41,542 --> 02:59:43,022
I'm already labelled.

2360
02:59:44,812 --> 02:59:46,121
(music turns menacing)

2361
02:59:50,724 --> 02:59:52,113
This is my label.

2362
02:59:55,896 --> 02:59:57,626
(upbeat music)

2363
03:00:10,776 --> 03:00:11,717
(music stops)

2364
03:00:12,192 --> 03:00:13,822
Who is Thiyagarajan, sir?

2365
03:00:16,632 --> 03:00:17,833
Ayya.

2366
03:00:18,216 --> 03:00:19,706
(intense music)

2367
03:00:44,838 --> 03:00:48,846
Before Ayya became a Label,
he committed two murders

2368
03:00:48,911 --> 03:00:50,722
as Advocate Thiyagarajan, and
it's the only case against him.

2369
03:00:50,788 --> 03:00:52,282
Later, he went underground.

2370
03:00:52,467 --> 03:00:53,858
For 16 years.

2371
03:00:54,130 --> 03:00:57,529
Recently, Minister Anbarasan's
brother-in-law Kanagaraj

2372
03:00:57,533 --> 03:00:58,791
was murdered in front
of Chennai Central, right?

2373
03:00:58,868 --> 03:01:00,730
It was Ayya who did it.

2374
03:01:04,228 --> 03:01:06,578
<i>After this incident, the minister
entered the scene.</i>

2375
03:01:06,587 --> 03:01:11,566
That's how everyone got to know
that Ayya is the head of the Label.

2376
03:01:17,049 --> 03:01:20,677
The police did not just get word
about Ayya through this murder.

2377
03:01:20,946 --> 03:01:22,357
But also his fingerprints.

2378
03:01:22,976 --> 03:01:25,477
So, the police has
Ayya's fingerprints.

2379
03:01:25,506 --> 03:01:27,816
But they still don't know
Ayya's identity.

2380
03:01:28,086 --> 03:01:29,736
The fingerprint didn't match

2381
03:01:29,920 --> 03:01:32,487
the government databases
or criminal records.

2382
03:01:32,735 --> 03:01:35,527
The police kept this top secret
for a long time, sir.

2383
03:01:35,755 --> 03:01:38,387
But recently, Ayya got to know
about this.

2384
03:01:41,449 --> 03:01:42,899
Even the police got to know
about this.

2385
03:01:42,938 --> 03:01:46,299
So, they sped up their search
to nab him quickly.

2386
03:01:46,307 --> 03:01:48,838
Moreover, there's political
pressure from the minister.

2387
03:01:48,946 --> 03:01:50,979
In all this, they made
only one mistake.

2388
03:01:54,273 --> 03:01:56,804
<i>Desperate to catch Ayya,</i>

2389
03:01:56,857 --> 03:02:00,915
they attached his name and
fingerprints to some false cases.

2390
03:02:00,948 --> 03:02:02,644
Since Ayya was a lawyer,

2391
03:02:02,684 --> 03:02:06,204
he has planned a few strategies to
come out of them with ease.

2392
03:02:06,402 --> 03:02:10,247
The plan is to come out of all
the false cases filed by the police,

2393
03:02:10,426 --> 03:02:14,285
and use that to claim the original
case as false and come out of it.

2394
03:02:19,627 --> 03:02:22,604
So, all he needs is a lawyer who can
break through all the false cases

2395
03:02:22,644 --> 03:02:23,985
that the police created.

2396
03:02:24,038 --> 03:02:25,705
That's the motive behind all this.

2397
03:02:25,733 --> 03:02:28,044
Paramasivan sir had a word with you.

2398
03:02:28,065 --> 03:02:33,265
Join the Label. You can sponsor
and run your own tournament.

2399
03:02:33,497 --> 03:02:35,553
The Bar Council filed a complaint
against you.

2400
03:02:35,566 --> 03:02:37,831
I'm a fraud? Who complained
against me, sir?

2401
03:02:38,084 --> 03:02:39,734
How can I say that, sir?

2402
03:02:39,753 --> 03:02:41,524
There's a complaint against you.

2403
03:02:41,542 --> 03:02:43,702
It'll be sorted once you prove
your innocence.

2404
03:02:43,727 --> 03:02:45,523
The case was filed through Arul Kumaran.

2405
03:02:45,705 --> 03:02:47,476
Contrary to what everyone thinks,

2406
03:02:47,737 --> 03:02:49,428
this murder wasn't
committed for the Label.

2407
03:02:49,674 --> 03:02:51,613
This was done to make you
a Label.

2408
03:02:51,642 --> 03:02:53,504
All this happened for that.

2409
03:02:55,017 --> 03:02:57,736
(dramatic music)

2410
03:03:03,815 --> 03:03:05,905
Sir, one more thing.

2411
03:03:05,990 --> 03:03:09,364
It wasn't Paathaalam's goons who tried
to kill your parents at the festival.

2412
03:03:09,441 --> 03:03:10,481
It was Ayya.

2413
03:03:12,287 --> 03:03:13,639
(knife slashes)

2414
03:03:25,126 --> 03:03:26,187
Motherfucker!

2415
03:03:26,415 --> 03:03:27,985
Let's see who wins.

2416
03:03:28,128 --> 03:03:29,793
The Label or the Law.

2417
03:03:34,270 --> 03:03:37,658
(Sukumar) <i>How do we find the Ayya
who no one has seen before, sir?</i>

2418
03:03:38,249 --> 03:03:42,057
(Prabha) <i>The fox hides only
as long as the forest is not on fire.</i>

2419
03:03:42,558 --> 03:03:45,385
<i>It will eventually come out.
I'll make it.</i>

2420
03:03:47,444 --> 03:03:49,174
(music rises)

2421
03:03:49,479 --> 03:03:54,320
(Subtitles by Desynova Digital)

2422
03:03:55,611 --> 03:03:57,590
(Paramasivan) <i>He is trying to destroy
the entire Label.</i>

2423
03:03:58,007 --> 03:03:58,925
(knife scrapes)

2424
03:03:59,050 --> 03:04:00,180
I'm scared.

2425
03:04:00,222 --> 03:04:01,203
(bike revs, tyres screech)

2426
03:04:01,351 --> 03:04:03,097
(Ayya) <i>No one should become
the next leader.</i>

2427
03:04:03,267 --> 03:04:04,259
(knife swishes)

2428
03:04:04,927 --> 03:04:07,074
(melancholic music)

2429
03:05:51,749 --> 03:05:53,709
He was fucking stabbed
in the middle of the road!

2430
03:05:53,752 --> 03:05:54,962
Instead of killing those bastards,

2431
03:05:55,224 --> 03:05:57,104
you're here to compete for
Paathaalam's seat?

2432
03:05:57,596 --> 03:05:58,707
Are you not ashamed?
(spits)

2433
03:06:00,255 --> 03:06:01,913
(celebratory cheering)

2434
03:06:01,953 --> 03:06:03,124
Bunk Suresh has been released.

2435
03:06:04,025 --> 03:06:07,254
Whoever fucking ends Bunk Suresh,
he will be the successor!

2436
03:06:07,994 --> 03:06:10,392
If someone's end can be brought
about by framing him,

2437
03:06:10,513 --> 03:06:13,185
<i>using the same case, the guy who
framed him can be finished too.</i>

2438
03:06:15,453 --> 03:06:16,528
Come to the Label.

2439
03:06:16,569 --> 03:06:19,749
You can sponsor your tournament
yourself and continue to run it.

2440
03:06:20,483 --> 03:06:23,024
I am part of a label.
This is my label.

2441
03:06:24,673 --> 03:06:28,921
We'll fucking see who wins.
The Label or the Law.

2442
03:06:34,522 --> 03:06:37,082
-(knife honing)
-(motorbike whirrs)

2443
03:06:48,782 --> 03:06:51,882
(inaudible dialogue)

2444
03:06:52,117 --> 03:06:53,132
(suspenseful music)

2445
03:07:19,623 --> 03:07:23,795
VAALI NAGAR PEOPLE'S LIBRARY

2446
03:07:23,873 --> 03:07:25,331
(music turns upbeat)

2447
03:07:38,711 --> 03:07:40,631
(Muthuvel) I've spoken to
Royapuram Guna as well, Prabha.

2448
03:07:40,819 --> 03:07:41,847
He has agreed to file a case.

2449
03:07:42,316 --> 03:07:44,516
Also, this is an IG case.

2450
03:07:45,054 --> 03:07:48,006
The IG is pressuring that
the accused has to be nabbed.

2451
03:07:48,561 --> 03:07:50,033
It's the case you started.

2452
03:07:50,231 --> 03:07:51,639
It'll be nice if you nab him for us.

2453
03:07:51,731 --> 03:07:53,830
It'll be a huge load off
of our shoulders.

2454
03:08:02,566 --> 03:08:04,194
(carrom coin strikes)

2455
03:08:06,908 --> 03:08:08,498
He needs to be taken out first.

2456
03:08:09,336 --> 03:08:10,376
What about them then?

2457
03:08:11,072 --> 03:08:12,623
He said that he'll handle it.

2458
03:08:13,102 --> 03:08:15,644
It's this motherfucking bastard
who's disturbing them a lot.

2459
03:08:15,660 --> 03:08:16,676
That's why.

2460
03:08:16,956 --> 03:08:18,396
He wants him killed
without any noise.

2461
03:08:22,354 --> 03:08:24,065
(opening song)

2462
03:08:34,841 --> 03:08:40,134
LABEL
WALK THE STAGE GLORIOUSLY

2463
03:08:47,083 --> 03:08:49,105
(phone ringing)

2464
03:08:53,213 --> 03:08:55,518
-Hello.
-<i>Thambi</i>, this is Sukumar.

2465
03:08:55,560 --> 03:08:56,957
-Do you remember me?
-<i>Anna.</i>

2466
03:08:56,975 --> 03:08:58,807
Come on, <i>anna</i>?
Of course, I remember, tell me.

2467
03:08:59,280 --> 03:09:02,312
Of the remaining four, there's one
who went missing as a young boy.

2468
03:09:02,645 --> 03:09:05,199
-<i>But the rest are in the Label.</i>
-(tyres screech)

2469
03:09:05,237 --> 03:09:06,965
<i>I couldn't ask around
about it very openly.</i>

2470
03:09:07,341 --> 03:09:09,149
Wait for a few days.
We'll get them.

2471
03:09:09,190 --> 03:09:11,120
Okay, <i>anna</i>.
Thank you.

2472
03:09:12,274 --> 03:09:13,442
What happened?

2473
03:09:13,479 --> 03:09:14,677
My bike has a flat tyre.

2474
03:09:14,719 --> 03:09:17,039
So, I'm trying to book an auto,
but I can't seem to find one.

2475
03:09:17,547 --> 03:09:18,697
Okay, come get in.

2476
03:09:19,416 --> 03:09:21,546
No, sir. I'll get it.
Seems like there's one nearby.

2477
03:09:21,588 --> 03:09:24,365
Hey, don't be stubborn.
Just get in.

2478
03:09:26,555 --> 03:09:28,041
-(truck honking)
-(vehicles whirring)

2479
03:09:36,865 --> 03:09:38,876
(sombre music)

2480
03:09:41,665 --> 03:09:44,703
Hey, I don't have to
justify this to you.

2481
03:09:46,247 --> 03:09:48,029
I saw this as my last bus.

2482
03:09:48,872 --> 03:09:51,822
If I missed it, I felt like I'd be
stranded here till the end.

2483
03:09:52,829 --> 03:09:53,909
So, I got in.

2484
03:09:55,627 --> 03:09:57,278
They've gotten down too, sir.

2485
03:09:57,943 --> 03:09:59,663
They won't get back in.

2486
03:09:59,703 --> 03:10:01,252
Don't put that weight on me.

2487
03:10:02,225 --> 03:10:03,636
If it's not me,
there'll be another lawyer.

2488
03:10:06,192 --> 03:10:07,971
It hurts because it's you.

2489
03:10:10,937 --> 03:10:12,175
Why, sir?

2490
03:10:12,673 --> 03:10:16,293
Was it all for this new car, office,
money and privilege?

2491
03:10:16,335 --> 03:10:17,687
Hey, don't say such cliched things.

2492
03:10:18,366 --> 03:10:20,347
I'm a lawyer.
I only did my job.

2493
03:10:21,332 --> 03:10:22,691
There are a lot of cases for that.

2494
03:10:22,743 --> 03:10:24,154
Why? Why not this case?

2495
03:10:26,345 --> 03:10:29,814
In that case, no lawyer should
represent anyone who did wrong.

2496
03:10:30,736 --> 03:10:31,767
Is that possible?

2497
03:10:34,593 --> 03:10:35,852
Was it for your mother, sir?

2498
03:10:38,178 --> 03:10:41,606
Why, sir? Won't I take care of
your mother's medical expenses?

2499
03:10:42,302 --> 03:10:44,410
Hey, I must take care of it.

2500
03:10:45,004 --> 03:10:46,161
You asshole!

2501
03:10:48,225 --> 03:10:51,024
I should earn and I should
take care of my mother.

2502
03:10:52,228 --> 03:10:54,716
Do you expect me to die
doing these petty cases?

2503
03:10:55,592 --> 03:10:56,843
No, sir.

2504
03:10:57,514 --> 03:11:01,242
Why? The case reached the hearing
because you took it up, right?

2505
03:11:03,059 --> 03:11:04,347
Why did you agree?

2506
03:11:07,340 --> 03:11:09,170
You had a reason, right?

2507
03:11:09,916 --> 03:11:13,007
Similarly, others can have
their reasons too.

2508
03:11:21,530 --> 03:11:22,551
(brakes screech)

2509
03:11:28,913 --> 03:11:30,814
Hey, wait for a minute.
I'll go in and just be back.

2510
03:11:30,856 --> 03:11:32,433
No, sir.
I'll get going now.

2511
03:11:32,531 --> 03:11:34,371
You wait.
I'll bring her.

2512
03:11:34,439 --> 03:11:36,290
Sir, I've asked Mahitha to come.

2513
03:11:38,233 --> 03:11:40,003
(firewood crackles)

2514
03:11:42,619 --> 03:11:46,296
(menacing music)

2515
03:11:58,892 --> 03:12:00,975
(gate creaks)

2516
03:12:09,157 --> 03:12:10,346
(man) <i>Anna.</i>

2517
03:12:13,229 --> 03:12:14,381
Hmm.

2518
03:12:18,059 --> 03:12:19,591
(man on phone) At the harbour?

2519
03:12:20,468 --> 03:12:21,708
Okay, I'll talk.

2520
03:12:21,799 --> 03:12:23,168
(music settles)

2521
03:12:24,605 --> 03:12:25,855
I'll call back later.

2522
03:12:27,728 --> 03:12:29,568
Hey, what?

2523
03:12:29,865 --> 03:12:30,885
Uh-uh.

2524
03:12:35,022 --> 03:12:36,071
What's the matter?

2525
03:12:37,755 --> 03:12:39,187
Bunk Suresh is coming out tomorrow.

2526
03:12:41,423 --> 03:12:42,443
What's the matter?

2527
03:12:43,680 --> 03:12:45,061
To sacrifice the chicken.

2528
03:12:45,789 --> 03:12:46,949
Chicken?

2529
03:12:48,850 --> 03:12:50,380
Should we fucking bust his balls?

2530
03:12:51,922 --> 03:12:52,951
That's what I wanted to tell <i>Anna</i>.

2531
03:13:01,747 --> 03:13:04,998
Paathaalam's place is for the person
who takes out Bunk Suresh, right?

2532
03:13:09,206 --> 03:13:10,984
(firewood crackling)

2533
03:13:12,531 --> 03:13:14,752
See that, <i>Amma</i>?
Everything is back to normal.

2534
03:13:15,130 --> 03:13:16,959
That's why you should take
your medicines properly.

2535
03:13:16,982 --> 03:13:19,004
-I'll take it from now.
-(Mahitha) He'll ensure everything's okay.

2536
03:13:20,119 --> 03:13:21,799
Prabha!
Mahitha!

2537
03:13:21,818 --> 03:13:22,745
-<i>Amma</i>!
-Hi, Aunty.

2538
03:13:22,783 --> 03:13:24,840
-How are you both?
-We're good. What happened to you?

2539
03:13:25,085 --> 03:13:26,707
Just got a master check-up done.

2540
03:13:26,970 --> 03:13:29,450
Well, why don't you come home
these days?

2541
03:13:29,513 --> 03:13:31,383
I will come.
Just that I'm stuck with work.

2542
03:13:31,594 --> 03:13:33,565
Okay, whatever it is,
you must definitely come.

2543
03:13:33,838 --> 03:13:34,265
Okay.

2544
03:13:34,299 --> 03:13:35,572
-We'll surely come.
-Please do.

2545
03:13:35,613 --> 03:13:37,224
I'll go get the car, <i>Amma</i>.

2546
03:13:37,710 --> 03:13:38,724
Okay.

2547
03:13:43,729 --> 03:13:44,737
What is it, <i>Amma</i>?

2548
03:13:44,976 --> 03:13:47,016
He has hired a nurse
to look after me.

2549
03:13:47,303 --> 03:13:50,073
He has also employed different people
for housework and cooking.

2550
03:13:50,371 --> 03:13:52,530
He has painted the house.
He cleared our debt.

2551
03:13:52,787 --> 03:13:55,526
He's even building a room
on the terrace for his office.

2552
03:13:55,963 --> 03:13:58,243
Isn't that good, <i>Amma</i>?
Just be happy.

2553
03:13:59,098 --> 03:14:00,606
That's not it.

2554
03:14:00,971 --> 03:14:03,523
I'm a bit... scared.

2555
03:14:09,708 --> 03:14:11,508
(scooter whirring)

2556
03:14:15,146 --> 03:14:16,968
Hey, what happened?

2557
03:14:17,629 --> 03:14:18,640
Nothing.

2558
03:14:19,561 --> 03:14:20,881
Then, why the long face?

2559
03:14:21,378 --> 03:14:22,498
Now?

2560
03:14:22,974 --> 03:14:24,425
It's still the same now.

2561
03:14:25,634 --> 03:14:29,135
Okay, so I'm starting a new show
on our channel.

2562
03:14:29,196 --> 03:14:31,184
It's called U3.
Tell me what that means.

2563
03:14:31,385 --> 03:14:32,422
Tell me yourself.

2564
03:14:32,748 --> 03:14:35,679
-U3: unknown, untold, unseen.
-Oh.

2565
03:14:35,720 --> 03:14:40,293
Stories that we've never seen,
heard or told before,

2566
03:14:40,581 --> 03:14:42,149
and the people involved in it.
That's the show.

2567
03:14:42,430 --> 03:14:44,117
Guess who the first guest
of the show is.

2568
03:14:44,491 --> 03:14:46,626
-Who is it?
-Take a guess.

2569
03:14:46,764 --> 03:14:49,295
(intense music)

2570
03:15:00,218 --> 03:15:01,370
(auto whirring)

2571
03:15:03,314 --> 03:15:05,135
(music intensifies)

2572
03:15:07,483 --> 03:15:08,684
(Mahitha) Well? Tell me.

2573
03:15:28,334 --> 03:15:29,357
Prabha?

2574
03:15:29,704 --> 03:15:30,735
What happened?

2575
03:15:30,914 --> 03:15:32,823
It's nothing. Don't stop the bike
and keep going straight.

2576
03:15:38,998 --> 03:15:40,620
(tyres screech)

2577
03:15:41,444 --> 03:15:42,473
(rousing music)

2578
03:15:49,312 --> 03:15:51,329
(water pump squeaks)

2579
03:16:04,884 --> 03:16:07,097
(car skidding)

2580
03:16:16,108 --> 03:16:17,769
(brakes screech)

2581
03:16:21,630 --> 03:16:23,308
(music intensifies)

2582
03:16:30,566 --> 03:16:31,569
Get down.

2583
03:16:38,768 --> 03:16:40,017
(knife swishes)

2584
03:16:56,238 --> 03:16:57,954
-(knife slashes)
-(men gasp in shock)

2585
03:17:00,414 --> 03:17:01,432
(rousing music)

2586
03:17:02,780 --> 03:17:03,782
-(knife twists)
-(man grunts in pain)

2587
03:17:08,332 --> 03:17:10,652
(music turns menacing)

2588
03:17:21,902 --> 03:17:22,933
(man 1) Fucking get him!

2589
03:17:22,995 --> 03:17:24,104
(knife swishes)

2590
03:17:24,352 --> 03:17:26,061
(man grunts)

2591
03:17:30,187 --> 03:17:31,349
(Kumar shouts)

2592
03:17:31,659 --> 03:17:32,758
(grunts)

2593
03:17:34,179 --> 03:17:35,539
(screams in pain)

2594
03:17:37,543 --> 03:17:38,605
-(knife swishes)
-(man grunts)

2595
03:17:40,669 --> 03:17:42,061
(screaming)

2596
03:17:42,157 --> 03:17:43,236
(grunts)

2597
03:17:44,264 --> 03:17:45,344
(grunts)

2598
03:17:45,360 --> 03:17:47,173
(groans in pain)

2599
03:17:50,044 --> 03:17:51,051
(Veera grunts)

2600
03:17:51,593 --> 03:17:52,706
(music turns sinister)

2601
03:17:53,926 --> 03:17:55,017
(man) Fucking catch him!

2602
03:17:58,485 --> 03:17:59,491
(man groans)

2603
03:17:59,852 --> 03:18:01,709
-(grunts)
-(knife slashes)

2604
03:18:13,854 --> 03:18:15,835
(Veera groans in rage)

2605
03:18:18,718 --> 03:18:20,449
-<i>Anna</i>?
-<i>Anna</i>?

2606
03:18:20,459 --> 03:18:22,429
(panting)

2607
03:18:23,897 --> 03:18:25,108
(music slows down)

2608
03:18:33,515 --> 03:18:34,534
Hey!

2609
03:18:35,953 --> 03:18:37,553
(Prabha) Don't! Hey!

2610
03:18:38,991 --> 03:18:40,052
(grunts)

2611
03:18:41,524 --> 03:18:42,884
(slashes)

2612
03:18:46,497 --> 03:18:47,505
(grunts)

2613
03:18:47,769 --> 03:18:48,734
(slashes)

2614
03:18:50,051 --> 03:18:52,051
(groans in pain)

2615
03:18:55,319 --> 03:18:56,677
-(knife slashes)
-(man grunts)

2616
03:18:57,105 --> 03:18:59,321
(groans)

2617
03:19:05,977 --> 03:19:08,056
(Kumar shouts in rage)

2618
03:19:14,012 --> 03:19:16,956
Fuckers! We wanted to get his ass
on the line,

2619
03:19:16,998 --> 03:19:19,558
and other assholes are lining up
with weapons to get slashed.

2620
03:19:19,911 --> 03:19:21,391
(Bunk Suresh laughs maniacally)

2621
03:19:22,172 --> 03:19:23,423
Motherfuckers!

2622
03:19:25,415 --> 03:19:28,734
Hey, next time, just go spit
into his ear.

2623
03:19:29,266 --> 03:19:31,576
Some other fucking wimps will
come in the middle and die.

2624
03:19:31,654 --> 03:19:33,354
(Veera, Bunk Suresh chuckling)

2625
03:19:38,957 --> 03:19:41,246
<i>Anna!</i>
<i>Anna</i>, just wait a minute.

2626
03:19:41,965 --> 03:19:43,526
(Veera) Prabha <i>anna</i>.

2627
03:19:45,266 --> 03:19:46,586
<i>Anna</i>, come.

2628
03:19:46,657 --> 03:19:47,823
Come, <i>anna</i>.

2629
03:19:48,009 --> 03:19:49,131
Just come.

2630
03:19:49,173 --> 03:19:51,092
<i>Anna</i>, this is Prabha.

2631
03:19:51,228 --> 03:19:53,268
The lawyer I told you about.

2632
03:19:56,110 --> 03:19:57,687
<i>Anna</i>, in the contractor case,

2633
03:19:57,728 --> 03:19:59,928
it was he who saved us
without getting us on records.

2634
03:20:00,117 --> 03:20:02,035
Ah! Yes, right.

2635
03:20:02,075 --> 03:20:03,105
Hello.

2636
03:20:03,110 --> 03:20:07,299
<i>Anna</i>, without him, we wouldn't
have made our way into the Label.

2637
03:20:07,421 --> 03:20:11,050
If an FIR was filed and
we were put in jail that day,

2638
03:20:11,057 --> 03:20:15,009
we would have been insulted for not
finishing the target and being jailed.

2639
03:20:15,259 --> 03:20:17,680
And then, you wouldn't have
seen us as a Label.

2640
03:20:19,220 --> 03:20:21,572
Is that why you went in so
vengefully and killed them all?

2641
03:20:22,814 --> 03:20:23,828
Thanks, man.

2642
03:20:24,301 --> 03:20:26,501
Both of them are skilled rogues.

2643
03:20:26,638 --> 03:20:27,718
Sharp boys.

2644
03:20:28,345 --> 03:20:29,817
You were right to save them.

2645
03:20:30,775 --> 03:20:32,695
Tell me whatever you want,
we can get it done.

2646
03:20:32,709 --> 03:20:33,724
What do you say?

2647
03:20:35,234 --> 03:20:37,775
So, why did you slash him
on his ass?

2648
03:20:37,963 --> 03:20:39,992
-<i>Anna</i>, it wasn't on purpose.
-Hey!

2649
03:20:40,034 --> 03:20:41,893
Wait, what do you mean
it wasn't on purpose?

2650
03:20:41,953 --> 03:20:43,500
Remember that Rajabahadur
we took out?

2651
03:20:43,542 --> 03:20:45,671
Even that day, he slashed him
exactly on the ass.

2652
03:20:45,705 --> 03:20:46,403
Hey!

2653
03:20:46,445 --> 03:20:49,916
-I'll fucking hit you!
-You did, you ass-slasher!

2654
03:20:50,015 --> 03:20:51,724
(Kumar) Hey! Wait, you fucking wimp!

2655
03:20:51,725 --> 03:20:54,047
-(Veera) Damn ass-slasher!
-(Kumar) <i>Anna</i>, I'll ass-kick him!

2656
03:20:54,272 --> 03:20:55,752
-(Veera) Hey!
-(Kumar) Hey, fucking stop there!

2657
03:20:55,872 --> 03:20:58,181
(Kumar) You can't get away from me!
Stop, you!

2658
03:20:58,415 --> 03:21:00,065
(Bunk Suresh) Stop! We've got work.

2659
03:21:05,487 --> 03:21:07,077
(vessels clatter)

2660
03:21:07,435 --> 03:21:09,755
-<i>Amma</i>?
-I'm out of <i>vadas</i>.

2661
03:21:12,634 --> 03:21:13,855
Veera?

2662
03:21:14,074 --> 03:21:15,193
(vessels clacking)

2663
03:21:17,931 --> 03:21:20,022
-(motorbikes whirring)
-(vessels clatter)

2664
03:21:21,901 --> 03:21:25,099
That has expired.
Leave.

2665
03:21:28,460 --> 03:21:30,400
(crows cawing)

2666
03:21:38,394 --> 03:21:40,245
Does your family know
you've come here?

2667
03:21:40,436 --> 03:21:41,748
No.

2668
03:21:42,409 --> 03:21:45,100
Were you the one who was speaking
to him on the phone every night?

2669
03:21:45,647 --> 03:21:47,060
Yes.

2670
03:21:48,251 --> 03:21:50,331
Do you know
what he's doing now?

2671
03:21:50,746 --> 03:21:52,175
Yes.

2672
03:21:52,183 --> 03:21:53,274
I know.

2673
03:21:54,023 --> 03:21:57,361
-Go. Make something of yourself.
-He'll change.

2674
03:21:57,368 --> 03:21:58,408
Like hell he will!

2675
03:21:58,729 --> 03:21:59,999
(emotional music)

2676
03:22:00,291 --> 03:22:01,641
Don't make me say things.

2677
03:22:01,685 --> 03:22:02,699
Get going!

2678
03:22:04,987 --> 03:22:06,369
I'll change him.

2679
03:22:06,635 --> 03:22:09,835
Why?
Is changing him your job?

2680
03:22:10,149 --> 03:22:11,741
Were you born for that?

2681
03:22:12,991 --> 03:22:15,241
Is marrying him
and reforming him your job?

2682
03:22:16,132 --> 03:22:17,772
Is that marriage or jail?

2683
03:22:19,345 --> 03:22:22,934
If I ever see you loafing around
in search of him,

2684
03:22:23,589 --> 03:22:25,637
even I won't know
what I'll hit you with!

2685
03:22:27,743 --> 03:22:29,535
Oh, stop it! Just leave!

2686
03:22:30,441 --> 03:22:31,510
Get going, girl!

2687
03:22:34,156 --> 03:22:36,818
(sniffles and weeps)

2688
03:22:37,385 --> 03:22:40,127
What's this, <i>akka</i>? Why are
you spoiling your own son's...

2689
03:22:40,511 --> 03:22:41,882
What about her life?

2690
03:22:42,434 --> 03:22:45,445
It's our fate that we have sons like
these, and we have to put up with it.

2691
03:22:46,018 --> 03:22:47,581
Why does she need to face the same?

2692
03:22:47,682 --> 03:22:49,209
She looks like a goddess.

2693
03:22:49,514 --> 03:22:51,753
Wasn't my suffering in my attempt
to reform his father enough?

2694
03:22:52,008 --> 03:22:53,586
Let the chain of suffering
end with me.

2695
03:22:53,607 --> 03:22:54,627
(music stops)

2696
03:22:57,044 --> 03:22:58,782
(exhales)

2697
03:22:58,793 --> 03:23:00,204
Ten years, <i>anna</i>.

2698
03:23:00,556 --> 03:23:01,596
Ten years.

2699
03:23:01,821 --> 03:23:03,661
They were always here at
the fucking entrance.

2700
03:23:05,006 --> 03:23:06,667
That's why now they've
stuffed our mouths.

2701
03:23:06,701 --> 03:23:07,704
(sniffs deeply)

2702
03:23:11,023 --> 03:23:15,325
If you rely on boys like these,
they'll get you one day.

2703
03:23:18,222 --> 03:23:20,131
If you must become like Paathaalam,

2704
03:23:21,991 --> 03:23:24,042
you must become Paathaalam.

2705
03:23:26,572 --> 03:23:27,720
Aadhi.

2706
03:23:28,424 --> 03:23:31,093
Yesterday, we lost 6 people
from our Label.

2707
03:23:33,328 --> 03:23:35,204
We must finish him.

2708
03:23:35,514 --> 03:23:36,604
I'll do it, <i>Anna</i>.

2709
03:23:36,940 --> 03:23:38,288
(sniffs)

2710
03:23:41,836 --> 03:23:42,839
(eerie music)

2711
03:23:55,943 --> 03:23:57,284
I'm asking you.

2712
03:23:58,611 --> 03:23:59,822
What?

2713
03:24:00,593 --> 03:24:02,153
I just wanted to see you.

2714
03:24:03,291 --> 03:24:07,321
Right, like you'll just see me
and walk away.

2715
03:24:12,089 --> 03:24:13,093
Hey!

2716
03:24:14,430 --> 03:24:15,741
Don't you start.

2717
03:24:17,651 --> 03:24:19,033
You're going overboard.

2718
03:24:20,009 --> 03:24:21,357
I have been observing you.

2719
03:24:23,143 --> 03:24:25,002
You've completely changed now,
haven't you?

2720
03:24:40,675 --> 03:24:43,526
What? Don't I look amazing?

2721
03:24:45,958 --> 03:24:47,622
I did see you that day.

2722
03:24:48,009 --> 03:24:50,587
You were walking around like
you achieved something great.

2723
03:24:52,509 --> 03:24:55,298
I'd have come that day to your
house and taken you around.

2724
03:24:56,374 --> 03:24:58,572
But you immediately...

2725
03:24:59,255 --> 03:25:00,695
That's why I didn't come.

2726
03:25:01,150 --> 03:25:02,362
(sniffles sadly)

2727
03:25:04,140 --> 03:25:06,249
(tuts) Hey!
What's the matter?

2728
03:25:06,509 --> 03:25:07,567
Tell me and leave.

2729
03:25:10,213 --> 03:25:13,805
What you did...
is the matter.

2730
03:25:17,191 --> 03:25:19,431
Think about it properly,
and tell me what your plans are.

2731
03:25:22,662 --> 03:25:24,991
Hey, you could just go to
that doctor--

2732
03:25:25,002 --> 03:25:26,494
I'll slap you!

2733
03:25:28,235 --> 03:25:31,795
(melancholic music)

2734
03:25:35,582 --> 03:25:36,774
(footsteps fading away)

2735
03:25:42,055 --> 03:25:43,655
Okay, sir.
I'll check and send it.

2736
03:25:44,876 --> 03:25:46,236
-So, Suresh.
-<i>Anna</i>?

2737
03:25:46,271 --> 03:25:48,190
Seems like you've been quite active
ever since you came out.

2738
03:25:48,935 --> 03:25:51,258
The real estate and harbour
that was in Paathaalam's control

2739
03:25:51,300 --> 03:25:52,871
is slowly coming under our control.

2740
03:25:52,912 --> 03:25:53,953
Yes, <i>anna</i>.

2741
03:25:54,497 --> 03:25:57,545
If this must continue,
there must not be a next leader.

2742
03:25:57,631 --> 03:26:01,601
<i>Anna</i>, I had a great plan to take
out that asshole Kokkithoppu Aadhi.

2743
03:26:02,260 --> 03:26:05,881
Since Paathaalam died, I think
everyone there is out of control.

2744
03:26:06,625 --> 03:26:09,457
So, these low-level thugs are
giving their lives up.

2745
03:26:11,317 --> 03:26:12,454
Just wait for a few more days.

2746
03:26:12,873 --> 03:26:15,601
Senguttuvan, Aadhi.
I'll take them all out.

2747
03:26:17,381 --> 03:26:18,952
Do you know Advocate Prabhakar?

2748
03:26:19,970 --> 03:26:21,000
I know, <i>anna</i>.

2749
03:26:21,171 --> 03:26:24,361
Through Veera and Kumar.
He's from my area.

2750
03:26:24,674 --> 03:26:26,165
He's one of us, <i> Anna </i>.
What is it?

2751
03:26:26,349 --> 03:26:27,960
(scoffs) One of us, you say?

2752
03:26:28,996 --> 03:26:30,716
(sinister music)

2753
03:26:35,023 --> 03:26:36,760
(bike throttles)

2754
03:26:36,937 --> 03:26:38,206
(bike screeches)

2755
03:26:39,164 --> 03:26:41,535
-What is it?
-You could stay home for a few days.

2756
03:26:42,092 --> 03:26:43,095
Okay, come.
Get on.

2757
03:26:43,864 --> 03:26:45,194
No, I'll go on my own.

2758
03:26:46,028 --> 03:26:47,759
<i>Anna</i>, get on.

2759
03:26:48,724 --> 03:26:50,233
It's okay.
I'll go by myself.

2760
03:26:50,863 --> 03:26:54,015
<i>Anna</i>, they're on
the lookout for you.

2761
03:26:54,023 --> 03:26:55,032
Come.

2762
03:26:55,606 --> 03:26:56,696
Prabha.

2763
03:26:57,711 --> 03:26:58,734
Go.

2764
03:27:02,705 --> 03:27:04,694
Keep our boys away from him.

2765
03:27:08,028 --> 03:27:09,780
(bike revs)

2766
03:27:11,083 --> 03:27:12,913
-Shall we go, <i>anna</i>?
-Let's go.

2767
03:27:15,553 --> 03:27:18,313
(suspenseful music builds up)

2768
03:27:20,301 --> 03:27:21,392
(car starts)

2769
03:27:38,540 --> 03:27:40,448
(foreboding music)

2770
03:27:44,557 --> 03:27:46,776
-You guys can go. I'll be okay.
-(car halts)

2771
03:27:47,602 --> 03:27:48,634
<i>Anna, anna</i>.

2772
03:27:48,676 --> 03:27:50,325
You go and come.
We'll wait.

2773
03:27:50,566 --> 03:27:51,766
Go ahead, <i>anna</i>.

2774
03:27:55,739 --> 03:27:56,752
(foreboding music fades)

2775
03:28:04,187 --> 03:28:06,196
(bikes start)

2776
03:28:17,046 --> 03:28:18,304
(car screeches)

2777
03:28:20,283 --> 03:28:21,885
Thanks, guys.
Okay, you guys can leave.

2778
03:28:22,398 --> 03:28:24,449
<i>Anna</i>, you go and come back.

2779
03:28:26,208 --> 03:28:28,280
Are you going to protect
the police station?

2780
03:28:28,836 --> 03:28:30,796
-Get going.
-<i>Anna</i>, we'll wait.

2781
03:28:30,884 --> 03:28:32,683
Hey! Leave, you guys.

2782
03:28:38,927 --> 03:28:40,555
What in the hell were you doing?

2783
03:28:40,648 --> 03:28:42,615
Fuckers! Just do what
you've been told to do.

2784
03:28:43,988 --> 03:28:45,959
(Suresh) Hey, don't spare
a single one of them!

2785
03:28:46,005 --> 03:28:47,227
Ask everyone.

2786
03:28:47,291 --> 03:28:49,171
(bikes approach)

2787
03:28:52,123 --> 03:28:54,094
<i>Anna</i>, they're here.

2788
03:28:54,218 --> 03:28:56,416
(music intensifies)

2789
03:28:58,825 --> 03:29:00,334
Come soon.

2790
03:29:10,049 --> 03:29:11,209
Where are you coming from?

2791
03:29:12,252 --> 03:29:13,602
We just dropped Prabha <i>anna</i>
and came here, <i>anna</i>.

2792
03:29:21,773 --> 03:29:22,872
Where did you drop him off?

2793
03:29:23,041 --> 03:29:24,521
At S-23 Station.

2794
03:29:24,671 --> 03:29:25,759
Damn you!

2795
03:29:29,707 --> 03:29:31,726
Do you know
what that son of a bitch did?

2796
03:29:32,690 --> 03:29:33,780
What, <i>anna</i>?

2797
03:29:35,664 --> 03:29:38,205
(rousing music)

2798
03:29:46,422 --> 03:29:48,320
He's trying to destroy
the Label entirely.

2799
03:29:50,823 --> 03:29:52,148
He got into a fight with Ayya,

2800
03:29:52,190 --> 03:29:54,069
went to the families of
all the dead victims,

2801
03:29:54,575 --> 03:29:57,783
and obtained a written statement that
Ayya is the reason for their deaths.

2802
03:30:04,113 --> 03:30:08,161
So far, there have always been cases
about personal fights and land issues.

2803
03:30:09,134 --> 03:30:12,886
Until now, there has never been
a case on anyone in the Label.

2804
03:30:14,360 --> 03:30:17,948
But today that dog has filed
a case against Ayya.

2805
03:30:20,336 --> 03:30:22,536
Tell me who the witness is.
I'll take him out.

2806
03:30:23,066 --> 03:30:25,826
It's a list of fucking 167 cases,
you asshole!

2807
03:30:26,636 --> 03:30:27,672
(rousing music intensifies)

2808
03:30:30,950 --> 03:30:32,333
(coughs)

2809
03:30:35,906 --> 03:30:38,637
(Paramasivan) <i>The real problem is
that everyone who filed the case</i>

2810
03:30:38,678 --> 03:30:41,606
<i>are the mothers, wives and sisters
of the members of the Label.</i>

2811
03:30:42,676 --> 03:30:45,796
He has picked out people
from both the Labels.

2812
03:30:50,510 --> 03:30:53,460
Whoever we lay our hands on,
the Label will be harmed.

2813
03:31:02,760 --> 03:31:06,968
We merely called that fucker
to break four fake cases.

2814
03:31:07,330 --> 03:31:12,199
Now, he's filing 167 unbreakable
cases and trying to screw our asses.

2815
03:31:14,721 --> 03:31:17,379
(music crescendos)

2816
03:31:44,720 --> 03:31:49,632
(Subtitles by Desynova Digital)

2817
03:31:49,661 --> 03:31:50,781
(Kumar) Hey!

2818
03:31:51,957 --> 03:31:54,467
They took them out knowing
they were from our Label, right?

2819
03:32:01,810 --> 03:32:03,189
This is the right time.

2820
03:32:03,224 --> 03:32:04,631
Prabha? Prabha?

